  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "عَنْهُ عَنِ ٱلْحَسَنِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ عَنْ كَرَّامٍ عَنِ ٱبْنِ أَبِي يَعْفُورٍ قَالَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "From him, from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī, from Karrām, from Ibn Abī Yaʿfūr, who said:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ ٱلسَّلَامُ عَنْ رَجُلٍ قَطَعَ إِصْبَعَ ٱمْرَأَةٍ، قَالَ: «تُقْطَعُ إِصْبَعُهُ حَتَّى يَنْتَهِيَ إِلَى ثُلُثِ ٱلْمَرْأَةِ، فَإِذَا جَازَ ٱلثُّلُثَ أُضْعِفَ ٱلرَّجُلُ»."
      "translations": {
        "en": "I asked Abū ʿAbdillāh عليه السلام about a man who cut off a woman’s finger. He said: “His finger is cut off until it reaches one-third of the woman; then when it exceeds one-third, the man is doubled.”"
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "This hadith states a legal ruling concerning retaliation in bodily injury between a man and a woman. It explains that equal retaliation applies up to one-third, and when that threshold is exceeded, the legal treatment of the man is doubled according to the ruling mentioned by Imam al-Ṣādiq عليه السلام.",
      "seo_question": "What is the ruling on qiṣāṣ when a man cuts off a woman’s finger?",
      "key_terms": {
        "قَطَعَ": "cut off or severed",
        "إِصْبَعَ": "a finger",
        "ٱمْرَأَةٍ": "a woman",
        "تُقْطَعُ": "is to be cut off in retaliation",
        "ثُلُثِ": "one-third",
        "جَازَ": "exceeded or went beyond",
        "أُضْعِفَ": "was doubled"
      }
    }
  },
